{"strongs": "H3289", "word": "יָעַץ", "translit": "ya.ats", "root": "יעף", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "advise, counsel", "definition": "יָעַץ verb advise, counsel (only twice in Hexateuch) (Aramaic יְעט ; Arabic exhort, admonish ) — Qal Perfect 3 masculine singular יָעַץ Isa 7:5 + 11 t.; יָעָ֑ץ Isa 14:27 + 2 t.; suffix יְעָצָ֑נִי Ps 16:7 יְעָצָהּ Isa 23:9 + יְעָצָהוּ Baer 2Chr 10:8 3 plural יָָֽעֲצוּ Ps 62:5 suffix יְעָצֻהוּ 1Kgs 12:8 + 2 t. (including 2Chr 10:8 , Baer יְעָצָ֑הוּ ); etc.; Imperfect אִיעֲצָה Ps 32:8 ( Ol Che אִיעָֽצְךָ ); אִיעָֽצְךָ Exod 18:19 ; Num 24:14 (not elsewhere Hexateuch), Jer 38:15 , compare also foregoing; אִיעָצֵךְ 1Kgs 1:12 Participle active יוֺעֵץ Isa 3:3 + 9 t.; construct יֹעֵץ Nah 1:11 , יוֺעֵץ 2Sam 15:2 יוֺעֲצֵךְ Mic 4:9 plural יוֺעֲצִים Job 12:17 + 3 t.; יֹעֲצִים Ezek 11:2 construct יֹעֲצֵי Isa 19:11 + 2 t., etc.; feminine singular suffix יוֺעַצְתּוֺ 2Chr 22:3 Passive participle feminine יְעוּצָה Isa 14:26 — advise, counsel , with accusative Isa 32:7 ; Isa 32:8 ; Isa 23:9 (subject ׳ י ) Mic 6:5 followed by בְּלִיַּ֫עַל Nah 1:11 ; Nah 7:5 (followed by עַל = against ), Nah 19:12 (followed by id. ), Nah 23:8 (followed by id. ), Hab 2:10 (followed by לְ ); often with accusative of congnate meaning with verb 2Sam 16:23 ; 2Sam 17:7 ; Ezek 11:2 followed by אֶל against Jer 49:20 ; Jer 50:45 (in both of ׳ י ); followed by עַל against Jer 49:30 ; Isa 19:17 (of ׳ י ); compare passive participle Isa 14:26 with accusative of congnate meaning with verb + suffix person 1Kgs 12:8 ; 1Kgs 12:12 ; 1Kgs 12:13 ; 2Chr 10:8 with accusative of person 2Sam 17:15 ; Ps 16:7 ; Exod 18:19 ; Num 24:14 (+ rel. clause) Jer 38:15 absolute (of ׳ י ) Isa 14:24 (c. adverb כאשׁר ), v Isa 14:27 of man 2Sam 17:15 ( כזאת וכזאת ), v 2Sam 17:21 ( ככה + על ); followed by infinitive Ps 62:5 ; 2Chr 25:16 (of אלהים ); followed by clause without connective 2Sam 17:11 followed by לְלֹא חָכְמָה Job 26:3 — אִיעֲצָה עליך עיני Ps 32:8 (see above). — Participle active as substantive = counseller , king's adviser 2Sam 15:12 ; 1Chr 27:33 ; 2Chr 22:4 ; 2Chr 25:16 ; Ezra 7:28 ; Ezra 8:25 ; Isa 19:11 so feminine 2Chr 22:3 probably also 1Chr 27:32 (|| אִישׁ מֵבִין יְסוֺפֵר ); compare Mic 4:9 , also Isa 1:26 (|| שֹׁפְטִים ), Job 12:17 (|| id. ); — in these three, of importance for people; so also Isa 3:3 ; Prov 11:4 = Prov 24:6 compare Job 3:14 , and particularly פֶּלֶא יוֺעֵץ Isa 9:5 wonder of a counsellor , of the ideal ruler predicated. More generally, counsellor, adviser Prov 15:22 בְּשֶׂכֶל ׳ יו 1Chr 26:14 (specific reason for title unknown); ׳ יֹעֲ שָׁלוֺם Prov 12:20 = prophet Isa 41:28 , nearly = agents (hired by adversaries of Judah) Ezra 4:5 . Niph`al (reflexive or reciprocal) Perfect נוֺעַץ Isa 40:14 נוֺעֲצוּ Ps 71:10 ; Ps 83:6 Imperfect וַיִּוָּעַץ 1Kgs 12:6 + 10 t.; יִוָָּֽעֲצוּ Isa 45:21 וַיִּוָָּֽעֲצוּ 2Chr 30:23 נִוָָּֽעֲצָה Neh 6:7 Participle plural נוֺעָצִים 1Kgs 12:6 + 4 t.; — consult together, exchange counsel , of king with advisers, followed by אֶתֿ 1Kgs 12:6 ; 1Kgs 12:8 = 2Chr 10:6 ; 2Chr 10:8 and so of ׳ י Isa 40:14 followed by אֶלֿ 2Kgs 6:8 ; 2Chr 20:21 followed by עִם 1Chr 13:1 ; 2Chr 32:3 absolute consider 1Kgs 12:28 ; 2Chr 25:17 ; 2Chr 30:2 compare 1Kgs 12:6 (followed by infinitive) = 2Chr 10:6 ; 1Kgs 12:9 (followed by Imperfect + ו subordinate) = 2Chr 10:9 in general consult, take counsel , absolute Prov 13:10 יַחְדָּו Ps 71:10 ; Neh 6:7 ; Isa 45:21 followed by לֵב יַחְדָּו (with heart together) Ps 83:6 nearly = determine , followed by infinitive 2Chr 30:23 . Hithpa`el Imperfect יִתְיָעֲצוּ Ps 83:4 conspire against, followed by עַל (|| יַעֲרִימוּ סוֺד על ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3636')\">BDB3636</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3289')\">H3289</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3635')\">BDB3635</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3637')\">BDB3637</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יָעַץ</bdbheb> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>advise, counsel</highli